  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Durability",
      "items": [
        "pueued owns every job, so a worker outlives the lead",
        "result.txt is published by atomic rename — its existence IS the completion signal",
        "Admission is tri-state: retry needs proof of non-submission, never a missing id"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Publication and recovery",
      "items": [
        "delegate-run preserves raw output BEFORE deciding, so publication is recoverable",
        "Publish only on adapter-confirmed success — never on the exit code, never on 'terminal'",
        "provider.exit and publish.exit are separate: a pending publish is not a failure"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Intent and providers",
      "items": [
        "The lead sets intent: model · permission · effort — adapters own the spelling",
        "An unsupported OR unverified config key fails the dispatch, never silently dropped",
        "GLM · DeepSeek · MiniMax need no adapter — they are base-URL swaps"
      ]
    }
  ]
